    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0687" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg591"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Woodford to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 53.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On October 28 instant I received from you a
                    telegraphic dispatch in cipher, which I translate as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodford</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Minister, Madrid:</hi></p>
                        <p>Send by mail full text of Sagasta manifesto June 24 last referred to in
                            Spanish answer.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sherman.</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>To-day I obtained from Señor Sagasta, president of the council of ministers, the
                    inclosed copies of the manifesto of the Liberals addressed to the nation and
                    signed by Praxedes M. Sagasta, dated Madrid, 24th June, 1897, and published in
                    El Correo, an evening paper of Madrid, on Thursday, June 24, 1897. In the
                    private note from Señor Sagasta accompanying these newspaper copies he states
                    that it was not an official document, only the manifesto of a party that was out
                    of power, and <pb facs="0688" n="592" xml:id="pg592"/> that there was not a
                    special edition made, and that it was made public through its publication in the
                    newspapers.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart L. Woodford.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d505-a1.xml" xpointer="d505-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
